**The 4 grade combos under $4K (all lab, all honest value):**

- **Combo 1 — Budget Floor:** [IGI E-VVS2 Excellent at $792](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29754536?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Four stones at this exact price. Max-value entry point.
- **Combo 2 — Max Color Budget:** [IGI D-VVS2 Excellent at $836](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29975675?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). D colorless at the floor. +$44 for the top color grade.
- **Combo 3 — Ideal Label + VVS1:** [IGI D-VVS1 Ideal at $1,222](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29977752?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Ideal cut label plus VVS1 clarity plus D colour, all under $1,300.
- **Combo 4 — Flawless Ideal:** [IGI D-IF Ideal at $1,868](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/30235061?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Internally Flawless + D color + Ideal cut, still under $2k.

→ Our pick: **Combo 3 — [D-VVS1 Ideal at $1,222](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29977752?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — max certificate, Ideal label, under $1,300 leaves $2,700 for the setting.

**Priority:** at 1.25ct, natural pricing has a floor so high ($8,000 minimum) that lab becomes the only sensible choice under $4K. The entire natural inventory sits above the budget target. Every combo under $4K is lab. Full detail further down.

## Expert Summary

1.25 carat marquise diamond price sits in a $792–$10,499 band in current certified market inventory. The lab floor is $792 for IGI E-VVS2 Excellent — 10x cheaper than the natural floor. Natural inventory at 1.25ct is thin (only 2 certified stones live) and expensive. Every under-$4K pick at this size is lab. The face-up measurements are 11.0 × 5.5 mm at a 2.00 length-to-width ratio — bigger than a 1.5 carat round diamond on face-up area.

I'm Farzana Hasan, a GIA-certified diamond expert. At 1.25ct, the budget-first conversation becomes a lab conversation. Natural stones at this carat tier price for buyers with $8,000+ to spend on the stone alone. For the sub-$4K ring budget, lab is the only honest answer. Full credentials at **[Diamond Critics](https://diamondcritics.com/about-farzana/)**. Our pillar **[marquise cut diamond guide](/marquise-cut-diamond)** covers every carat tier.

This guide covers the full certified market audit at 1.25ct marquise natural (2 stones) and lab (14 stones), the 4 grade combos under $4K ranked by value, the Lab-Only Window framework, the Clarity Compression Zone concept, and the setting math that turns a $800 stone into a $5,000-looking ring. All prices are live affiliate links. Pricing presented as independent market research.

