## The Clarity Compression Zone — Why VVS2 to IF Costs Peanuts at 1.25ct

**The Clarity Compression Zone is the price band where the gaps between clarity grades compress to tiny dollar amounts.** At 1.25ct lab, VVS2 to VVS1 is a $270 step. VVS1 to IF is a $646 step. VS2 clarity does not exist in current certified lab inventory at 1.25ct — the market jumps directly from VVS2 up.

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Clarity (1.25ct D color Ideal)</th><th>Price</th><th>Visible Difference?</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>D-VVS2 Excellent</strong></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29975675?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$836</a></td><td>Baseline — loupe-only</td><td>The clarity floor for lab at 1.25ct. VVS2 is well beyond naked-eye detection.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>D-VVS1 Ideal</strong></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29977752?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$1,222</a></td><td>None to the eye</td><td>+$386 for VVS1 + Ideal cut combo. Jump covers two cert upgrades.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>D-IF Ideal</strong></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/30235061?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$1,868</a></td><td>None to the eye</td><td>+$646 for Internally Flawless. Compression zone peaks here.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>D-FL Ideal</strong></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29314684?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$2,037</a></td><td>None to the eye</td><td>+$169 over IF for Flawless. Microscope-only distinction.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** The Clarity Compression Zone at 1.25ct lab means every grade step costs under $700. That is unusual — on natural 1.25ct, each clarity step runs $2,000+. For lab buyers, the compression means picking VVS1 or IF over VVS2 is a reasonable budget decision, not a reckless one. The $500–$1,200 saved from skipping Combo 4 funds a stronger setting.

