<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Spec</th><th>1ct Marquise</th><th>1.25ct Marquise</th><th>1.5ct Marquise</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Face-up (mm)</strong></td><td>10.0 × 5.0</td><td>11.0 × 5.5</td><td>12.0 × 6.0</td><td>1.25 is 10% larger than 1ct, 9% smaller than 1.5ct.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Face-up area (mm²)</strong></td><td>39.3</td><td>47.5</td><td>56.5</td><td>Area jump 1→1.25 is bigger than 1.25→1.5. Diminishing returns above 1.5.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Natural floor price</strong></td><td>$4,049</td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29609846?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$8,000</a></td><td>~$8,500</td><td>1.25 natural costs almost same as 1.5 natural. Thin inventory penalty.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Lab floor price</strong></td><td>$629</td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29754536?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$792</a></td><td>~$1,100</td><td>Lab scales fair across all three tiers.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Reads as (face-up)</strong></td><td>1.25ct round</td><td>1.5ct round</td><td>2ct round</td><td>1.25 marquise reads as 1.5 round. 1.5 marquise reads as 2 round.</td></tr></tbody></table>

